<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (Hi, I'm Himanshu Verma, a student from India passionate about open source and building systems that last. I started coding at 14, roughly 4 years ago, and the way it started was unglamorous: I wrote a switch-case chain inside a loop, looked at it, and thought wait, how does AI actually do this? That one question sent me down a rabbit hole I haven't climbed out of since.)
/E (Hi, I'm Himanshu Verma, a student from India passionate about open source and building systems that last. I started coding at 14, roughly 4 years ago, and the way it started was unglamorous: I wrote a switch-case chain inside a loop, looked at it, and thought wait, how does AI actually do this? That one question sent me down a rabbit hole I haven't climbed out of since.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (Around the same time I had a laptop sitting around, downloaded Ubuntu, and spent weeks trying every popular Linux distro I could find. That's when open source hit me. I looked at Linux and thought: thousands of people built this, for free, and just gave it away. That was the coolest thing I had ever seen.)
/E (Around the same time I had a laptop sitting around, downloaded Ubuntu, and spent weeks trying every popular Linux distro I could find. That's when open source hit me. I looked at Linux and thought: thousands of people built this, for free, and just gave it away. That was the coolest thing I had ever seen.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (I completed my school CS curriculum early and built a strong foundation in Java. I primarily work in Unix environments and have been using open source tools like Git and Linux in my daily workflow for the past 3+ years. My knowledge base now includes Java, C, C++, Python, and JavaScript, and I am aspiring to be tech stack agnostic. If it compiles, I can work with it.)
/E (I completed my school CS curriculum early and built a strong foundation in Java. I primarily work in Unix environments and have been using open source tools like Git and Linux in my daily workflow for the past 3+ years. My knowledge base now includes Java, C, C++, Python, and JavaScript, and I am aspiring to be tech stack agnostic. If it compiles, I can work with it.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
