<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (Hacktoberfest was the turning point from using open source to contributing to it. I found it online, decided to try it, and what I got out of it wasn't just merged PRs. It was the discipline of writing clean commits, handling review feedback, and making changes without breaking what already works. Since then I've been contributing consistently, most notably to Apache HugeGraph, where I've submitted 13 pull requests with 11 merged across the core server and hugegraph-doc repositories.)
/E (Hacktoberfest was the turning point from using open source to contributing to it. I found it online, decided to try it, and what I got out of it wasn't just merged PRs. It was the discipline of writing clean commits, handling review feedback, and making changes without breaking what already works. Since then I've been contributing consistently, most notably to Apache HugeGraph, where I've submitted 13 pull requests with 11 merged across the core server and hugegraph-doc repositories.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
