/P 141 0 R
/E (Injects interrupt checks directly into loops and method calls at the bytecode level during compilation, providing CPU exhaustion control at the script level rather than relying solely on the server-level evaluationTimeout wall clock. The existing evaluationTimeout remains as an outer safety net. The interaction between bytecode interrupts and async traversal execution across server-managed threads must be validated.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
