<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (Attached to CompilerConfiguration at engine creation. Blocks dangerous language constructs at parse time: import statements, package declarations, class definitions, and reflection expressions. Method calls remain permitted since Gremlin traversals are expressed as method chains. This eliminates entire exploit categories before type analysis.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (Enforces allowed package allowlist at compile time: org.apache.tinkerpop.gremlin.* and org.apache.hugegraph.* graph APIs only. Anything outside produces a compile error. Risk note: because g and graph are injected as runtime bindings in HugeScriptTraversal, compatibility between static type checking and the dynamic DSL must be validated. Overly strict checking may break legitimate traversals and requires iterative tuning.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
621 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (Injects interrupt checks into loops and method calls at the bytecode level during compilation. Provides CPU exhaustion control at the script level rather than relying solely on the server-level evaluationTimeout wall clock. The existing evaluationTimeout remains as an outer safety net. The interaction between bytecode interrupts and async traversal execution across server-managed threads must be validated.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
