627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (The current checkXxx\(\) methods intermix Gremlin detection with backend-specific allowlists for MySQL, HBase, Cassandra, Raft, SofaRPC, and snapshot operations inside the same conditional chains. The refactoring extracts a dedicated GremlinSecurityPolicy class that encapsulates all Gremlin-specific enforcement decisions. HugeSecurityManager delegates Gremlin decisions to this class, creating a clear class boundary between Gremlin policy and backend policy. GremlinSecurityPolicy can be disabled independently when the compile-time sandbox is active. Backend protections covering socket access, network connections, and filesystem access for backends are preserved unchanged and continue to be enforced at runtime. Compile-time enforcement via the sandbox stack becomes the primary boundary. HugeSecurityManager remains as a fallback runtime guard during the transition period, covering reflection edge cases, native calls, and ClassLoader behavior that static analysis cannot fully address. Java 17 deprecates SecurityManager for removal, so the refactoring also prepares non-Gremlin protections for eventual migration.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
